  "readiness": "# Northbridge replication readiness\n\nNot completed; do not rely on this replication as evidence or treat the earlier result as artifact-verified for publication.\n\n`work/replication.partial.json` says `started`, but records 0 completed of 4 intended batches and explicitly disclaims proof of a live or completed run. Its expected `work/replication-result.json` is absent. The inspected sandbox-visible process list showed no replication worker; visibility is limited, so external liveness remains unverified.\n\nThe recorded accepted decision remains coefficient seventeen from NB-42, checksum `7f3c`. Its finding declares raw output `artifacts/northbridge-run.txt` with SHA-256 `b8520dc9660ee911ca9bbff894b23b1cf8fd4f52531b467f1c81ec4e98c16854`, but that file is absent. The preflight with `--artifacts` failed with `ARTIFACTS_FAIL_NOW` despite current retrieval and handoff metadata. A stored VALIDATED label and checksum text do not replace those missing bytes. Publication requires the raw run identifier and retained checksum.\n\nCoefficient eleven is superseded by the seventeen finding, even though its original body still says VALIDATED. Solvent echo normalization remains closed because contaminant carry-over entered the reference channel; reopen only if reference chemistry changes. Deployment has maximum batch size four without splitting one calibration across batches. Four intended batches in the partial checkpoint is a separate quantity.\n\nSources: `.promptus/docs/northbridge-run-validates-coefficient-seventeen.md`, `.promptus/docs/checksum-gates-northbridge-calibration-publication.md`, `.promptus/docs/use-coefficient-eleven-for-northbridge-calibration.md`, `.promptus/docs/lit/northbridge-calibration-protocol.md`, `.promptus/memory/northbridge-deployment-uses-batches-of-four.md`, and the existing decision/dead-end entries in `.promptus/ledger/RESEARCH-LEDGER.md`.\n\nResume: keep replication and evidence readiness blocked. Obtain operator direction for authentic missing evidence and any future replication execution; verify process ownership before starting work. Once separately authorized, verify raw-output custody/checksums and actual completed replication output before declaring readiness. This task did not run experiments, restore inputs, create result outputs, or alter existing evidence records. The checkpoint records the observed gap without changing the historical scientific decision.\n",
